<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chanthaburi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chanthaburi is a city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> near the Cambodian border, long known for its gem trade and fruit orchards. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1767, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a> seized the town and used it as the base where he gathered troops and built a fleet before driving the Burmese from the Ayutthaya region. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> occupied Chanthaburi from 1893 to 1905 as security for a treaty with Siam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chanthaburi.jpg" alt="Chanthaburi" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ajtnk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chanthaburi_City.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
